==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Devil Wife|Devil Wives]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*6 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Xenobeast Bunaglios]] spawns as the boss after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*1 [[Crocodylidae Kurocroc]] spawns after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*4 [[Formicidaean Ariant]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 93.33~100 seconds<sup>2,800f~3,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
While on paper this stage looks incredibly difficult, featuring annoying peons, Formicidaean Ariants disrupting your meatshields, and a duo of Xenobeast Bunaglios and Kurocroc wiping out everything, it's actually decently relaxed. That said, it is by no means easy. Depending on your unit choices, cash management can be a significant issue, and Bunaglios' [[Critical Hit]]s, combined with unfavorable [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]] dodge RNG and poorly placed Devil Wife [[Death Surge]]s can give you a very hard time. Regardless, [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] and Cat Egg Pod excel at stalling nearly every enemy here, since most of them are [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoths]]. Using [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], you can gradually chip down both Crocodylidae Kurocroc and Xenobeast Bunaglios. With precise timing, this stage becomes much more manageable.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]]: Naala can be cycled to deal incredibly high chip damage to every enemy in this stage, if your Wallet permits it. Despite its relatively long cooldown, Naala remains an incredible pick for this stage.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]]: Although his [[Surge Attack]] spawn radius is inconsistent, Doron has the potential to deal extremely high Kamikaze DPS. Also, his low cost means there is no drawback to use him whenever he is off cooldown. Don't forget that Wild Doges are immune to Surge Attacks.
*[[Ancient Egg: N111 (Super Rare Cat)|Cop Cat]]: With his [[Strong Against|Strong Against]] [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] and [[Behemoth Slayer]] abilities, Cop Cat excels at handling both Wild Doges and Formicidaean Ariants, even when weakened by Kurocroc. Additionally, his high HP allows him to tank multiple hits from various enemies in this stage.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Just as in previous stages, Cyberpunk can be utilized as a [[Long Distance]] crowd-control unit. However, he is expensive to deploy, so be sure to protect him well.
*[[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Kinjirou Cat]]: Since the two major threats of this stage happen to be [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] and [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] respectively, Kinjirou Cat does well to stall them during periods of downtime. He can also act as a phenomenal general meatshield for other units, since he can typically survive at least one Bunaglios attack.
*[[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]]: With nearly all of the main threats being Behemoth enemies, Cat Egg Pod can tank and dodge powerful attacks from the two bosses and the peons, rendering himself near-immortal. Watch out for the Devil Wives, which can chip down his health quickly, by using disposable attackers.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Aer (Uber Rare Cat)|Aervantex]]: Aervantex's high effective HP against Bunaglios, quick attack rate, and exceptional forward piercing range via Long Distance make them effective at handling every threat in this stage, provided they are kept well protected. However, Aervantex is allowed only one reposition, so try your best to prevent Wild Doges and Devil Wives from entering their blind spot.
*[[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bazifenix]]: A very strong nuker against Aliens. Can be cycled like Naala, except its effective HP allows it to stay on the field for a much longer time. With [[Strengthen]] [[Talents|Talent]], Bazifenix is able to deal upwards of 500k DPH to Xenobeast Bunaglios.
*[[Adventurer Kanna (Uber Rare Cat)|Fabled Adventurer Girl Kanna]]: Due to her [[Massive Damage]] vs. Dark enemies, Behemoth Slayer and Long Distance attacks, Kanna is remarkably well-suited for sniping Crocodylidae Kurocroc; Against Dark Behemoths, her damage is multiplied by 10x, skyrocketing her usual 10.2k DPH, to an absolutely ludicrous 102k DPH at level 50. She also has a 100% chance to spawn a level 3 Surge Attack which is almost guaranteed to hit right around when Kurocroc typically is, dealing excellent collateral damage. She won't survive very long, so time her well.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]: He needs to be protected exceptionally well because he barely outranges Bunaglios' [[Explosion]]s, but if he is well protected, he does amazingly. His [[Wave Attack]]s will nearly 1-shot the Wild Doges and Ariants and can also kill them if also get hit by his initial attack. He can also kill the Devil Wives easily, if his Wave hits one that's far enough, she might not even hit any units with [[Death Surge]]. Be careful of the Ariants burrowing into him, or Devil Wives sniping him with Death Surge, those are the only threats other than Bunaglios.
*[[Komori (Uber Rare Cat)|Moririn]]: Resists both Bunaglios and Crocodylidae Kurocroc with Behemoth Slayer, boasting 787,500 effective HP against them. Their conjure can be used as an emergency escape button as well! Try to mitigate as many hits as possible from other enemies here, as they will quickly shred this Pixie.

